  "evidence": "TEXT_F: Mandatory National Service at 18; 8,000 more neighbourhood police, hotspot policing, facial recognition and tighter protest controls; harsher sentences and four new prisons; defence spending to 2.5% and a Veterans Bill; legal, binding annual migration cap with higher salary thresholds, Rwanda flights and the Illegal Migration Act; NHS funding uplift, Pharmacy First, new GP surgeries and Community Diagnostic Centres; welfare reforms with tighter assessments, tougher sanctions and a new Fraud Bill; Tobacco and Vapes Bill; clarify Equality Act with “sex” meaning biological and single‑sex accommodation rights.\n\nTEXT_G: Right to see a GP within 7 days, 8,000 more GPs, mental health hubs and urgent dentistry access; free personal care, a Carer’s Minimum Wage and stronger carers’ rights; scrap the benefit cap and two‑child limit, extend free school meals and a plan to end rough sleeping; liberalise immigration/asylum (scrap Illegal Migration Act and Rwanda, safe/legal routes, flexible visas, lift work ban); rights and democratic reform (retain HRA/ECHR, votes at 16, PR, digital rights, regulate biometrics, ban conversion practices); strong environmental and water protections; defence spending towards 2.5% and community policing with guaranteed burglary response.",
